      "text": "True",
      "quote": {
        "author": "XFreeze",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1876785200010539008/2_HFJjq9_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-06 00:23:48",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-05T16:23:48.000Z",
        "id": "2118378758147297681",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWX-P3yb0AAjKiv.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 1200,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWX-P3yb0AAjKiv.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1200
          }
        ],
        "name": "X Freeze",
        "text": "Starlink is becoming a GAME CHANGER for airlines, driving higher customer satisfaction, stronger loyalty and even influencing which airline passengers choose to fly with\n\nAnd the numbers are absolutely extraordinary:\n\n• United Airlines — Customers are choosing United specifically because of Starlink, with the airline seeing opportunities to turn them into long-term loyal passengers\n\n• Alaska/Hawaiian — Guest satisfaction is 20% higher on Starlink-equipped flights, while nearly 75% of non-members using the onboard portal signed up for Atmos Rewards\n\n• Virgin Atlantic — Onboard connectivity satisfaction has increased by more than 40 points, with Starlink also helping attract new Flying Club members\n\n• airBaltic — Net Promoter Scores are approximately 9 points higher on Starlink-equipped flights\n\n• ZIPAIR — Passenger revenue grew 12.3% YoY, with JAL highlighting fleetwide Starlink connectivity alongside flexible pricing\n\nStarlink has become a real competitive advantage, improving the passenger experience, strengthening customer loyalty, and giving people another reason to choose which airline they fly with\n\nThe future of in-flight connectivity is becoming a major part of how airlines compete",
        "url": "https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2118378758147297681",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
